Feature: Acceptance - application availability
  The deployed app must actually serve its API before we ship it anywhere

  Background:
    Given "curl" is installed
    And the following profile:
      | name    | value                         |
      | apphost | http://localhost:8090/student |

  Scenario: The students API endpoint answers with HTTP 200
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl --silent --show-error --fail --output /dev/null --write-out "HTTP %{http_code}" <apphost>/students/getAllStudents
      """
    Then the output should contain:
      """
      HTTP 200
      """

  Scenario: The API documentation (Swagger UI) is served
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl --silent --show-error --fail --output /dev/null --write-out "HTTP %{http_code}" <apphost>/swagger-ui/index.html
      """
    Then the output should contain:
      """
      HTTP 200
      """
